<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Ablation Study (RQ2)</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify the independent contributions of each component, we designed a bottom-up ablation study (Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.3 Ablation Study (RQ2) ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ AIR-VLA+: Decoupling Movement and Manipulation via Cascaded Dual-Action Decoders with Asymmetric MoE for Aerial Robots" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S4.T2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Detailed Ablation Study.</span> Experiments verify the independent contributions of the compressed global semantic features, visual perception, the stop-gradient operation, and multi-expert routing modules.</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T2.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:48.6pt;vertical-align:-23.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-217.5pt,30.7pt) scale(0.442300778935313,0.442300778935313) ;">
